y. Ensure that you continue to use the todo list to track your progress. Please proceed with the current tasks if applicable\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"69efb05e-bf98-4f4c-9bcd-7c6193285013\",\"uuid\":\"fc5cb977-9a55-42a5-afe5-efd6ac567484\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"oldTodos\":[{\"content\":\"Resolve merge conflicts in __init__.py and cli.py\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"activeForm\":\"Resolving merge conflicts\"},{\"content\":\"Delete temporary .prompt files\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"activeForm\":\"Deleting temporary files\"},{\"content\":\"Read referenced spec and code files\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"activeForm\":\"Reading spec and code files\"},{\"content\":\"Create human-inputs/ directory structure\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"activeForm\":\"Creating directory structure\"},{\"content\":\"Implement se3 human input --file command\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"activeForm\":\"Implementing human input file command\"},{\"content\":\"Implement se3 human input --list command\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"activeForm\":\"Implementing human input list command\"},{\"content\":\"Add tests for human input functionality\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"activeForm\":\"Adding tests\"},{\"content\":\"Run tests and commit\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"activeForm\":\"Running tests and committing\"}],\"newTodos\":[{\"content\":\"Resolve merge conflicts in __init__.py and cli.py\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"activeForm\":\"Resolving merge conflicts\"},{\"content\":\"Delete temporary .prompt files\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"activeForm\":\"Deleting temporary files\"},{\"content\":\"Read referenced spec and code files\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"activeForm\":\"Reading spec and code files\"},{\"content\":\"Create human-inputs/ directory structure\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"activeForm\":\"Creating directory structure\"},{\"content\":\"Implement se3 human input --file command\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"activeForm\":\"Implementing human input file command\"},{\"content\":\"Implement se3 human input --list command\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"activeForm\":\"Implementing human input list command\"},{\"content\":\"Add tests for human input functionality\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"activeForm\":\"Adding tests\"},{\"content\":\"Run tests and commit\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"activeForm\":\"Running tests and committing\"}]}}\n   179→{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"msg_Z9f2m8oQzPtqGrYIsofDhict\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Task completed. Here's a summary of what was accomplished:\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nSuccessfully resolved merge conflicts and completed the human input implementation for task-005:\\n\\n### Changes Made:\\n1. **Resolved merge conflicts** in:\\n   - `tools/se3_tools/__init__.py` - Combined version comment to include both human-calls and human-input commands\\n   - `tools/se3_tools/cli.py` - Added imports and registration for both `human_calls_cmd` and `human_input` modules\\n\\n2. **Added missing file** from master:\\n   - `tools/se3_tools/commands/human_calls_cmd.py` - Provides `se3 human-calls archive` and `se3 human-calls list` commands\\n\\n3. **Cleaned up**:\\n   - Deleted all temporary `.prompt` files\\n\\n### Verification:\\n- All 42 tests pass (21 human_input tests + 21 human_calls tests)\\n- `se3 human --list` shows pending inputs\\n- `se3 human input --file <path>` reads and processes input files\\n- `se3 human-calls archive/list` work correctly\\n- `se3 openspec` commands work correctly\\n\\nThe implementation supports file-based human input as an alternative to MCP calls, with:\\n- `human-inputs/` directory structure with `archive/` subdirectory\\n- Input file format with Context, Request, and Response sections\\n- Archival of processed input files\\n- Listing pending input files\"}],\"model\":\"kimi-for-coding\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":63818,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":0,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"prompt_tokens\":63818,\"cached_tokens\":0},\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"69efb05e-bf98-4f4c-9bcd-7c6193285013\",\"uuid\":\"68aa409c-2dd5-4520-894b-37369c577f4b\"}\n   180→{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"duration_ms\":220293,\"duration_api_ms\":236365,\"num_turns\":74,\"result\":\"Task completed. Here's a summary of what was accomplished:\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nSuccessfully resolved merge conflicts and completed the human input implementation for task-005:\\n\\n### Changes Made:\\n1. **Resolved merge conflicts** in:\\n   - `tools/se3_tools/__init__.py` - Combined version comment to include both human-calls and human-input commands\\n   - `tools/se3_tools/cli.py` - Added imports and registration for both `human_calls_cmd` and `human_input` modules\\n\\n2. **Added missing file** from master:\\n   - `tools/se3_tools/commands/human_calls_cmd.py` - Provides `se3 human-calls archive` and `se3 human-calls list` commands\\n\\n3. **Cleaned up**:\\n   - Deleted all temporary `.prompt` files\\n\\n### Verification:\\n- All 42 tests pass (21 human_input tests + 21 human_calls tests)\\n- `se3 human --list` shows pending inputs\\n- `se3 human input --file <path>` reads and processes input files\\n- `se3 human-calls archive/list` work correctly\\n- `se3 openspec` commands work correctly\\n\\nThe implementation supports file-based human input as an alternative to MCP calls, with:\\n- `human-inputs/` directory structure with `archive/` subdirectory\\n- Input file format with Context, Request, and Response sections\\n- Archival of processed input files\\n- Listing pending input files\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"session_id\":\"69efb05e-bf98-4f4c-9bcd-7c6193285013\",\"total_cost_usd\":2.126715700000001,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":54135,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":3405568,\"output_tokens\":5266,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"modelUsage\":{\"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\":{\"inputTokens\":54135,\"outputTokens\":5266,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":3405568,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":0,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":2.105109000000001,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000},\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\":{\"inputTokens\":10880,\"outputTokens\":1319,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":41317,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":0,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.021606699999999993,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000}},\"permission_denials\":[],\"uuid\":\"d068e7f2-4d1f-41d1-81b6-97da26471e06\"}\n   181→\n   182→\n   183→## Instructions\n   184→Analyze the event and decide the next action. Respond ONLY with valid JSON matching this schema:\n   185→{\n   186→  \"action\": \"plan|merge|reject|retry|split|escalate|complete\",\n   187→  \"tasks\": [...],\n   188→  \"target_task\": \"task-id\",\n   189→  \"merge_branch\": \"branch-name\",\n   190→  \"retry_prompt\": \"adjusted prompt for retry\",\n   191→  \"reason\": \"explanation\",\n   192→  \"summary\": \"human-readable summary of decision\"\n   193→}\n   194→\n   195→Rules:\n   196→- For 'plan': include full task definitions in 'tasks' array\n   197→- For 'merge': set target_task and merge_branch\n   198→- For 'reject': set target_task and reason (becomes feedback for worker retry)\n   199→- For 'retry': set target_task and retry_prompt\n   200→- For 'split': set target_task and new sub-tasks in 'tasks'\n   201→- For 'escalate': set reason (will be sent to human)\n   202→- For 'complete': when all tasks are merged and done\n   203→- If unsure, use 'escalate' rather than guessing\n   204→\n   205→CRITICAL CONSTRAINTS:\n   206→1. You have LIMITED turns (30 max) - use tools efficiently, decide quickly\n   207→2. Your FINAL message must contain ONLY a valid JSON object with an \"action\" field\n   208→3. No markdown, no explanation, no analysis text — ONLY the JSON object\n   209→4. DO NOT use TodoWrite or other tools in your final turn - output JSON directly\n   210→5. If you cannot complete research in time, use \"action\": \"escalate\" with reason\n   211→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c77ebd74-ac41-45b7-bb22-47a1590f2ed7","uuid":"2fb768a1-3ae8-4763-8001-31030d5ccd1e","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/data/cre/workspace/se3.0/tmpcf2zye7t.prompt","content":"# Manager Agent Rules\n\nYou are a MANAGER agent in an SE3 git-worktree collaboration session.\nYou are invoked on-demand by the orchestrator to make decisions. You are NOT resident — you read state from `.collab/`, decide, output JSON, and exit.\n\n## Your Scope\n\nYou handle strategic decisions. You do NOT:\n- Write implementation code\n- Run tests directly\n- Manage git worktrees or branches (the orchestrator does this)\n- Interact with users directly (use `ask_human` MCP tool if needed)\n\n## Decision Types\n\nYou respond to events with ONE of these actions:\n\n| Action | When to Use |\n|--------|-------------|\n| `plan` | Initial task decomposition. Break the objective into parallel tasks. |\n| `merge` | Worker completed, code looks good. Approve the merge. |\n| `reject` | Worker completed, but code has issues. Provide specific feedback. |\n| `retry` | Worker failed, but the task is retryable. Provide adjusted guidance. |\n| `split` | Task is too large or complex. Break it into smaller sub-tasks. |\n| `escalate` | You cannot resolve the issue. Route to human. |\n| `complete` | All tasks are merged and the objective is fulfilled. |\n\n## Response Format\n\nYou MUST respond with valid JSON only. No markdown, no explanation outside JSON.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"plan|merge|reject|retry|split|escalate|complete\",\n  \"tasks\": [],\n  \"target_task\": \"task-id\",\n  \"merge_branch\": \"branch-name\",\n  \"retry_prompt\": \"adjusted prompt\",\n  \"reason\": \"explanation\",\n  \"summary\": \"human-readable summary\"\n}\n```\n\n## Task Decomposition Rules (for `plan` action)\n\n1. **Maximize parallelism**: Tasks that touch different files/modules should be separate\n2. **Minimize dependencies**: If task B depends on task A's output, note this — the orchestrator merges A first\n3. **Bounded scope**: Each task should be completable in one session (< 60 minutes)\n4. **Clear spec references**: Each task must reference the spec files the worker needs to read\n5. **Self-contained prompts**: The worker has NO context beyond the prompt you write and the files in its worktree. Include everything it needs.\n\n### Task Definition Format\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"task-001\",\n  \"branch\": \"collab/short-description\",\n  \"worktree\": \".worktrees/short-description\",\n  \"status\": \"pending\",\n  \"title\": \"Human-readable title\",\n  \"prompt\": \"Full, detailed prompt for the worker. Include: what to implement, which files to read, which specs to follow, what tests to write.\",\n  \"spec_refs\": [\"openspec/specs/relevant-spec/spec.md\"],\n  \"dependencies\": [],\n  \"health\": {\n    \"timeout_minutes\": 60,\n    \"attempts\": 0,\n    \"max_attempts\": 3\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Code Review Rules (for `merge` / `reject` decisions)\n\nWhen reviewing a completed worker's branch:\n\n1. **Check the diff summary** — does it match the task scope? No unrelated changes?\n2. **Check test results** — did the worker run and pass tests?\n3. **Check spec compliance** — does the implementation satisfy the spec scenarios?\n4. **Check for regressions** — any obvious issues in the diff?\n\nApprove (`merge`) unless there are clear problems. Don't reject for style nitpicks.\nReject (`reject`) with specific, actionable feedback the worker can act on.\n\n## Failure Handling Rules\n\n- **Timeout**: If the worker timed out, consider: Was the task too large? → `split`. Was the prompt unclear? → `retry` with better prompt. Repeated timeout? → `escalate`.\n- **Error exit**: Read the worker log. Identify the root cause. If fixable by retry with guidance → `retry`. If systemic → `escalate`.\n- **Blocked**: Worker couldn't proceed without information. Can you answer from context? If yes → `retry` with the answer included in prompt. If no → `escalate` to human.\n\n## Merge Order\n\nWhen multiple branches are ready for merge:\n1. Foundational/infrastructure changes first\n2. Changes that other tasks depend on\n3. Independent feature changes (any order)\n4. Changes that modify the same files as already-merged branches go LAST (higher conflict risk)\n\n## MCP Tools Available\n\n- **ask_human(question, options?, urgent?)** — Escalate to human when you cannot make a decision. Use sparingly.\n- **notify_human(message, level)** — Inform human of significant events (all tasks done, critical failure, etc.)\n\n## What NOT to Do\n\n- Do NOT guess when unsure — use `escalate`\n- Do NOT approve merges without reviewing the diff summary\n- Do NOT create tasks with vague prompts — workers have zero context beyond what you write\n- Do NOT retry indefinitely — respect max_attempts\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\nProject root: /data/cre/workspace/se3.0\nBase branch: master\n\n## All Tasks\n{\"id\": \"task-001\", \"branch\": \"collab/openspec-cli-commands\", \"worktree\": \".worktrees/openspec-cli-commands\", \"status\": \"failed\", \"title\": \"Implement OpenSpec CLI commands (init, list)\", \"prompt\": \"Implement the `openspec` CLI commands referenced in session-protocol spec but missing from the codebase.\\n\\n**Background**: The session-protocol spec (openspec/specs/session-protocol/spec.md) references `openspec init` and `openspec list --specs` commands in the startup protocol, but these commands don't exist. The se3 scaffold commands exist but not the openspec-specific commands.\\n\\n**What to implement**:\\n1. Add `openspec init` command - Initialize the openspec/ directory structure (similar to what se3 init does but focused on openspec/)\\n2. Add `openspec list --specs` command - List all available specs in openspec/specs/\\n\\n**Files to read**:\\n- openspec/specs/session-protocol/spec.md (lines 9-30 for startup protocol)\\n- openspec/specs/se3-scaffold/spec.md (for reference on init behavior)\\n- tools/se3_tools/commands/init.py (see how se3 init works)\\n- tools/se3_tools/cli.py (see CLI structure)\\n\\n**Implementation details**:\\n- The openspec commands can be subcommands of se3 OR a separate openspec CLI\\n- `openspec init` should create openspec/specs/, openspec/changes/, openspec/changes/archive/ directories\\n- `openspec list --specs` should list all specs in openspec/specs/ with their purposes\\n- Follow the existing command pattern in tools/se3_tools/commands/\\n\\n**Tests**: Add tests in tests/ directory following existing patterns.\\n\\n**Do NOT modify**: The session-protocol spec itself - only implement the missing commands it references.\", \"spec_refs\": [\"openspec/specs/session-protocol/spec.md\", \"openspec/specs/se3-scaffold/spec.md\"], \"dependencies\": [], \"health\": {\"timeout_minutes\": 60, \"attempts\": 1, \"max_attempts\": 3, \"last_activity\": \"2026-02-18T17:24:35.941449\"}, \"started_at\": \"now\", \"worker_pid\": 2472034, \"worker_exit_code\": 1, \"completed_at\": \"now\"}\n{\"id\": \"task-002\", \"branch\": \"collab/spec-purpose-updates\", \"worktree\": \".worktrees/spec-purpose-updates\", \"status\": \"done\", \"title\": \"Fill in TBD Purpose fields for three specs\", \"prompt\": \"Update the Purpose fields for three specs that currently have \\\"TBD - created by archiving change\\\" placeholders.\\n\\n**Specs to update**:\\n1. **spec-lint** (openspec/specs/spec-lint/spec.md) - Currently line 4 has \\\"TBD - created by archiving change toolize-se3. Update Purpose after archive.\\\"\\n2. **requirement-intake** (openspec/specs/requirement-intake/spec.md) - Currently line 4 has \\\"TBD - created by archiving change requirement-capture. Update Purpose after archive.\\\"\\n3. **change-verifier** (openspec/specs/change-verifier/spec.md) - Currently line 4 has \\\"TBD - created by archiving change toolize-se3. Update Purpose after archive.\\\"\\n\\n**How to determine the Purpose**:\\nRead each spec's Requirements section and understand what it governs. Write a clear 1-2 sentence Purpose that explains:\\n- What this spec defines/controls\\n- Why it exists in the SE3 framework\\n\\n**Example good Purpose** (from session-protocol):\\n\\\"Define the session lifecycle protocol for SE 3.0 agents. This spec governs progressive startup, execution boundaries, shutdown procedures, and tool-enforced progress tracking across sessions.\\\"\\n\\n**Files to read**:\\n- openspec/specs/spec-lint/spec.md (read full file to understand its purpose)\\n- openspec/specs/requirement-intake/spec.md (read full file to understand its purpose)\\n- openspec/specs/change-verifier/spec.md (read full file to understand its purpose)\\n\\n**What to edit**:\\nOnly update the \\\"## Purpose\\\" section in each of the three spec files. Do not change any other content.\\n\\n**Verification**: Run `se3 lint` after changes to ensure specs are still valid.\", \"spec_refs\": [\"openspec/specs/spec-lint/spec.md\", \"openspec/specs/requirement-intake/spec.md\", \"openspec/specs/change-verifier/spec.md\"], \"dependencies\": [], \"health\": {\"timeout_minutes\": 30, \"attempts\": 1, \"max_attempts\": 3, \"last_activity\": \"2026-02-18T17:35:59.691789\"}, \"started_at\": \"now\", \"worker_pid\": 2472064, \"worker_exit_code\": 1, \"completed_at\": \"now\", \"review\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}}\n{\"id\": \"task-003\", \"branch\": \"collab/human-calls-archive\", \"worktree\": \".worktrees/human-calls-archive\", \"status\": \"done\", \"title\": \"Implement human calls archiving system\", \"prompt\": \"Implement an archiving system for completed human calls.\\n\\n**Background**: The human-as-mcp spec defines async human calls stored in `human-calls/` directory. Currently there's no system to archive completed calls - they just accumulate in the main directory.\\n\\n**What to implement**:\\n1. Create `human-calls/archive/` directory structure\\n2. Add `se3 human-calls archive` command that:\\n   - Moves completed human calls (those with Response sections filled) to human-calls/archive/\\n   - Preserves the original filename format: `{YYYYMMDD}-{HHmmss}-{description}.md`\\n   - Optionally supports `--dry-run` to preview what would be archived\\n3. Add `se3 human-calls list` command that:\\n   - Lists pending (unresponded) human calls\\n   - Lists recently archived calls\\n4. Update `se3 collab --status` to show pending human calls count (mentioned in issues.md)\\n\\n**Files to read**:\\n- openspec/specs/human-as-mcp/spec.md (understand human call format)\\n- tools/se3_tools/human_calls.py (existing human call utilities)\\n- tools/se3_tools/commands/collab.py (see how --status works)\\n- tools/se3_tools/commands/status.py (for reference on status display)\\n\\n**Human call file format**:\\nFiles in human-calls/ have Request and Response sections. A call is \\\"completed\\\" when the Response section has content.\\n\\n**Implementation notes**:\\n- Add the new commands to tools/se3_tools/commands/ (create human_calls.py or similar)\\n- Register commands in cli.py\\n- Follow existing patterns for CLI output and error handling\\n- Add tests in tests/ directory\\n\\n**Do NOT modify**: The human-as-mcp spec itself - only implement the archiving functionality.\", \"spec_refs\": [\"openspec/specs/human-as-mcp/spec.md\"], \